{
  "format": "srwb",
  "version": "1.0",
  "notebook": {
    "name": "TypR Introduction",
    "cells": [
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "# TypR — Typed R\n\nTypR is a typed superset of R that compiles to standard R code.\nIt adds type annotations, type checking, and generics while\nkeeping full R compatibility.\n\n**Note:** TypR requires semicolons at the end of statements.",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "let x <- 42;\ncat(\"x =\", x, \"\\n\");",
        "language": "typr",
        "name": "basics"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "let add <- function(a, b) a + b;\ncat(\"3 + 4 =\", add(3, 4), \"\\n\");",
        "language": "typr",
        "name": "functions"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "let greeting: char <- \"Hello from TypR!\";\nprint(greeting);",
        "language": "typr",
        "name": "typed"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "let square <- function(x) x * x;\nlet result <- square(7);\ncat(\"7 squared =\", result, \"\\n\");",
        "language": "typr",
        "name": "square"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "## Directives\n\nUse `#!show-r` in a cell to toggle viewing the generated R code.\nUse `#!typecheck` followed by code to type-check without executing.\nUse `#!transpile` followed by code to see the transpiled R output.",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "#!transpile\nlet fib <- function(n) {\n  if (n <= 1) n\n  else fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)\n};\ncat(fib(10));",
        "language": "typr",
        "name": "transpile_demo"
      }
    ]
  }
}
